  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="c5ef-e204-2a0d-d478" name="Hittite (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>HITTITE ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.6-7), also usable for Mitannian, Syrian, Canaanite or Hyksos armies.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Chariotry at least a quarter of the points; Infantry up to half; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to half.
Hittite three-man chariots: Movement 7, Strength 4. A chariot may have three crew (+1 Attacks, +5 pts) or carry a chariot runner as a passenger.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Chariotry: at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
